# {{ project_id }}

ROS 2 {{ ros_distro }} project using the Docker image `{{ img_id }}`.

## Build the image

The image user must use the same numeric UID and primary GID that own the host workspace:

```bash
cd docker
python3 build.py developer "$(id --user)" "$(id --group)"
```

The primary group name defaults to the user name. Use `--group GROUP_NAME` when the names must differ.

## Run the project

Create one environment file for each deployment machine. The identity helper copies the user information stored in the selected image; then you add the host paths and device values required by `docker-compose.yaml`.

```bash
cd docker
python3 robotics_dockers_user_env.py {{ img_id }} \
    --output env_files/production.env

# Edit env_files/production.env before starting the project.
docker compose \
    --env-file env_files/production.env \
    --file compose_files/docker-compose.yaml \
    up -d
```

An environment file may be versioned when it contains shared machine settings and no passwords, tokens or other secrets. The workspace is mounted at `/workspace` inside the container.

## Workspace

- `src/0_deps/` contains repositories imported from `deps.repos`.
- `src/bringup/` contains launch, configuration and visualization resources.
- `src/simulation/` contains simulation-specific resources.
- `docker/` contains the image build context and production Compose files.
